  "interpretation": [
    "Both experiments use the same frozen chronological training/evaluation population.",
    "R1 achieves higher Top-K accuracy than the current MOD-007 historical-similarity ranking formulation at K=1, 3, 5, and 10.",
    "MOD-007 provides ranking-native MRR and NDCG metrics, which R1 does not provide.",
    "Both approaches show strong historical-support dependence: performance increases substantially as the target assignee has more training-period examples.",
    "Singleton and low-support assignees remain difficult for both approaches, while high-support assignees account for substantially stronger performance.",
    "The current MOD-007 result does not justify selecting the current similarity-plus-assignee-aggregation formulation over R1 on Hit@K.",
    "The evidence does justify investigating a modified ranking scoring or aggregation strategy rather than repeating the same MOD-007 formulation.",
    "Unseen evaluation targets remain genuine open-world cases and are not converted into ordinary negatives.",
    "No conclusion about operational assignee eligibility or universal routing correctness is made from these historical evaluation results."
